# Feature description: Logarithm of the COMPACTNESS feature to account for nonlinear relationships. 
# Usefulness: Since COMPACTNESS has a wide range and its values are skewed, applying a log transformation can normalize its distribution, potentially improving model performance by capturing interactions better.

df['LOG_COMPACTNESS'] = df['COMPACTNESS'].apply(lambda x: np.log(x))
end

python
# Step 2: Create a ratio feature between MAX.LENGTH_RECTANGULARITY and PR.AXIS_RECTANGULARITY
# Feature name: RECTANGULARITY_RATIO
# Feature description: Ratio of MAX.LENGTH_RECTANGULARITY over PR.AXIS_RECTANGULARITY to capture relative rectangular qualities of the silhouette.
# Usefulness: This feature can better highlight the relative variance in rectangular geometries for different vehicle types and help distinguish shape properties based on perspective.

df['RECTANGULARITY_RATIO'] = df['MAX.LENGTH_RECTANGULARITY'] / df['PR.AXIS_RECTANGULARITY']
end

python
# Step 3: Apply z-score standardization for SCALED_RADIUS_OF_GYRATION
